SHIPJIN PUMSE

02:30.880 --> 02:34.880
SHIPJIN PUMSE

02:34.880 --> 02:38.880
SHIPJIN PUMSE

02:56.880 --> 03:02.880
SHIPJIN PUMSE consists of 10 key moves, namely HWANGSOMAKI.

03:04.880 --> 03:08.880
SHIPJIN PUMSE

03:34.880 --> 03:38.880
SHIPJIN PUMSE

03:54.880 --> 04:00.880
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of SHIPJIN PUMSE.

04:00.880 --> 04:06.880
HWANGSOMAKI is a technique used to move the two outer wrists up to block simultaneously.

04:06.880 --> 04:12.880
Twist your wrist so that the back of the fist faces downward at the lower abdomen.

04:12.880 --> 04:18.880
Raise your fists up to your face, then snap your elbow to block upward.

04:18.880 --> 04:24.880
When blocking, the fist should be placed obliquely above the elbow.

04:24.880 --> 04:30.880
The space between the back of the wrist and forehead should be about one raised fist length.

04:30.880 --> 04:34.880
The distance between the fists should be the same.

04:36.880 --> 04:42.880
Close both your elbows and chest to stabilize the shoulders and shoulder blades.

04:42.880 --> 04:46.880
Keep the arms that performed HWANGSOMAKI firm.

04:48.880 --> 04:52.880
Close your chest and be mindful not to let your elbow open backwards.

04:55.880 --> 05:01.880
SONPADAK KODORO PAKATMAKI is a technique used to perform ANPARMOK PAKATMAKI

05:01.880 --> 05:05.880
by placing the whole palm of the other hand on the outer wrist.

05:05.880 --> 05:12.880
This technique is typically used to perform a strong block with assistance from one arm against a strong attack,

05:12.880 --> 05:15.880
then quickly connect to the next move.

05:15.880 --> 05:20.880
The tip of the middle finger of the opposite hand starts at the wrist of the blocking arm.

05:21.880 --> 05:25.880
Next, gather all your fingers and attach them to the outer wrist.

05:25.880 --> 05:30.880
Both elbows should face downward, and the armpits should be touching the body.

05:32.880 --> 05:36.880
The armpit of the assisting arm should not be away from the body.

05:37.880 --> 05:46.880
PYEONSUNGKUD OPPO CHIRIGI is a technique to strike at an opponent's pressure points

05:46.880 --> 05:51.880
by gathering the four fingers straight with the palm facing downward.

05:51.880 --> 05:57.880
You can attack a pressure point with a strong force as the contact surface of the target becomes smaller

05:57.880 --> 06:00.880
when struck with your gathered four fingers.

06:02.880 --> 06:05.880
This move transfers a strong force.

06:05.880 --> 06:11.880
Be careful to keep the four fingers aligned to avoid injuries to the finger joints.

06:14.880 --> 06:18.880
Pay attention to keeping the fingers gathered to protect the joints

06:19.880 --> 06:26.880
and be careful not to let the elbow open outside in order to perform OPPO CHIRIGI accurately.

06:27.880 --> 06:38.880
PAWIMIRGI is a technique where you open your hands and gather them at the back, twist back,

06:38.880 --> 06:42.880
then push in a straight line using your palms.

06:46.880 --> 06:50.880
Bend the wrists naturally and keep your thumb close to your hand.

06:51.880 --> 06:58.880
Your left arm is placed obliquely with a space of one hand span between the back of your hand and forehead.

06:59.880 --> 07:06.880
Your right hand is symmetrically placed slightly below your left hand with a one-fist space between.

07:08.880 --> 07:15.880
Opening the elbow weakens the shoulder, so exert force while you tighten the elbows and straighten the body.

07:16.880 --> 07:22.880
Perform this move slowly, exerting force on the lower abdomen with your eyes forward.

07:24.880 --> 07:29.880
The elbows should not open backwards, the torso must not tilt to one side,

07:31.880 --> 07:35.880
and the wrist and elbow should not be straight when the move is completed.

07:36.880 --> 07:46.880
SONNADUNG HECHOMAKKI is a technique used to block inside out by opening the two hands using the back of the hand blade.

07:47.880 --> 07:56.880
You can use the back of the hand blade to strike and block, absorb and block, and wind and grab an opponent's arm.

07:56.880 --> 08:01.880
Your elbow should face downward, and your armpit should lightly touch the body.

08:03.880 --> 08:06.880
The tip of your hand must not rise above your shoulder.

08:07.880 --> 08:12.880
Your armpit should not open due to your elbow rising or moving far away from the body.

08:13.880 --> 08:16.880
The back of your hand blade must go outside the shoulder line.

08:17.880 --> 08:25.880
KURO OREGI is a technique used to block outside out by opening the two hands using the back of the hand blade.

08:26.880 --> 08:31.880
The back of the hand blade should face upward or brush aside an opponent's attack using the inner wrist.

08:33.880 --> 08:37.880
The arm performing KURO OREGI comes near the body from below.

08:38.880 --> 08:41.880
The wrist is then twisted so the inner wrist faces upward.

08:42.880 --> 08:44.880
Then the back of it is snapped to block.

08:45.880 --> 08:48.880
The arm is not the only part used to perform this move.

08:49.880 --> 08:52.880
The flexible movement of the arm and back must also be in harmony.

08:53.880 --> 08:57.880
The opposite arm is pulled to the back at the same speed and force.

08:58.880 --> 09:03.880
The upper body must be flexible, and the lower body must stand firm.

09:05.880 --> 09:08.880
The wrist should cross the center line,

09:11.880 --> 09:16.880
and the space between the torso and arm should be about one raised fist's length.

09:17.880 --> 09:23.880
Be careful not to let the arm performing KURO OREGI pass the waist and fall back.

09:24.880 --> 09:25.880
Then pull up.

09:28.880 --> 09:36.880
CHITTARI CHIRIGI is a technique used to thrust forward with the two fists using the torque of the torso from CHAGEN DOLJOKUI.

09:37.880 --> 09:43.880
Maintain a space of about two fists' length between the fists and thrust at the solar plexus level.

09:43.880 --> 09:45.880
Your arm should be parallel.

09:47.880 --> 09:55.880
The fist in the back should be placed on the wrist of the other arm in APKUBI and placed on the elbow of GIKUBI.

09:56.880 --> 10:03.880
The elevation of the two arms must be identical, and the fists should not be placed apart too wide or narrow,

10:04.880 --> 10:07.880
maintaining a space of about two fists' length between them.

10:08.880 --> 10:16.880
PYEONSON EOKGURO ARERIMAKI is a technique to block above or below by opening the hand and crossing the wrists.

10:17.880 --> 10:24.880
The main reason for opening the hands is to deter an opponent's attack early and connecting to JAPGI.

10:25.880 --> 10:29.880
Tighten your elbows and lightly attach your armpits on your body.

10:30.880 --> 10:40.880
SONNADEUNG KODOROMAKI is a technique used mainly to grab an opponent and connect to another move, or to absorb and block.

10:41.880 --> 10:46.880
Perform BAKKANMAKI with a hand blade with the palm of the blocking hand facing upward

10:47.880 --> 10:52.880
and make the back of the assisting hand faced upward so the wrist and center line cross.

10:52.880 --> 10:57.880
Remember that the back of the assisting hand, not the palm, should face upward.

10:58.880 --> 11:03.880
The space between the assisting arm and torso should be about one hand length.

11:05.880 --> 11:07.880
KODORO DDUNGJUMOK APCHIGI

11:08.880 --> 11:10.880
Make a fist with the assisting arm.

11:11.880 --> 11:14.880
Bend the arm and place it behind the ear level.

11:15.880 --> 11:19.880
The fist performing DDUNGJUMOK APCHIGI should be placed behind the ear level.

11:19.880 --> 11:26.880
The fist performing DDUNGJUMOK APCHIGI should be placed so the arm is parallel to the opposite side of the chest.

11:27.880 --> 11:32.880
And the APCHIGI is performed with both arms moving forward along with the spin of the torso.

11:34.880 --> 11:38.880
The fist should be at the philtrum level during DDUNGJUMOK APCHIGI.

11:39.880 --> 11:45.880
The assisting hand should be at the solar plexus level with the back of the fist facing downward and the arm horizontal.

11:46.880 --> 11:49.880
These are the 10 key moves of SHIPJIN PUMSAE.

11:51.880 --> 11:55.880
We will now look at the moves in succession, connecting each move.

11:58.880 --> 12:03.880
The key moves of SHIPJIN FIRST PART consist of HWANG SOMAKKI.

12:07.880 --> 12:11.880
SONBADA KODORO WEN AN PALMOK BAKKATMAKKI.

12:11.880 --> 12:12.880
HWANG SOMAKKI

12:13.880 --> 12:15.880
ORIUN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI

12:21.880 --> 12:22.880
And DOUBLEJIRUGI

12:24.880 --> 12:25.880
HAECHEO SANTEULMAKKI

12:27.880 --> 12:28.880
ORIUN YEOPJIRUGI

12:32.880 --> 12:33.880
And MUNGAEJIGI

12:35.880 --> 12:39.880
SONBADA KODORO WEN AN PALMOK BAKKATMAKKI

12:40.880 --> 12:42.880
ORIUN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI

12:44.880 --> 12:45.880
And DOUBLEJIRUGI

12:46.880 --> 12:47.880
HAECHEO SANTEULMAKKI

12:48.880 --> 12:49.880
ORIUN YEOPJIRUGI

12:51.880 --> 12:52.880
And MUNGAEJIGI

12:54.880 --> 12:58.880
Before performing SONBADA KODORO WEN AN PALMOK BAKKATMAKKI,

12:59.880 --> 13:04.880
spread the two fists that performed HWANG SOMAKKI about a face length apart.

13:05.880 --> 13:11.880
Then pause for a while and connect to SONBADA KODORO WEN AN PALMOK BAKKATMAKKI.

13:12.880 --> 13:18.880
We will take a look at the ORIUN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI and DOUBLEJIRUGI moves in succession.

13:19.880 --> 13:22.880
Open your left fist and twist inward.

13:23.880 --> 13:26.880
Then transition from ORIUN KWIKKUBI to WEN APKUBI.

13:28.880 --> 13:32.880
Connect the DOUBLEJIRUGI following the ORIUN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI.

13:35.880 --> 13:37.880
We will now look at each move separately.

13:40.880 --> 13:42.880
Exert force on the hand making a fist.

13:43.880 --> 13:45.880
Then slowly open the four fingers.

13:47.880 --> 13:50.880
Bend your wrist inward when all fingers are open.

13:51.880 --> 13:53.880
With force still exerted on the right hand,

13:54.880 --> 13:58.880
move it to the back of your hand when the left wrist is completely twisted.

13:59.880 --> 14:03.880
Brush the right palm on the back of the left hand to perform JIRUGI.

14:05.880 --> 14:08.880
This is how the upper body should move during this time.

14:09.880 --> 14:11.880
Your right foot remains in place,

14:12.880 --> 14:16.880
and your left foot transitions to APKUBI while performing PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI.

14:17.880 --> 14:22.880
Next, quickly connect from PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI to DOUBLEJIRUGI.

14:22.880 --> 14:26.880
Remember that the spin of the left hand and the opening of the fist,

14:27.880 --> 14:30.880
the moving of the right hand over the back of the left hand,

14:31.880 --> 14:33.880
must occur simultaneously while breathing.

14:36.880 --> 14:38.880
When performing HECHO SANTERUMAKI,

14:39.880 --> 14:41.880
set your right foot forward.

14:42.880 --> 14:44.880
When performing ORIUN YOPJIRUGI,

14:45.880 --> 14:48.880
move your left foot and assume the front GOASOGI posture.

14:48.880 --> 14:51.880
Set your right foot forward to assume the JUCHUMSOGI posture.

14:52.880 --> 14:56.880
Then complete the YOPJIRUGI by pulling an opponent as if to cover

14:57.880 --> 15:00.880
and pull them downward with the left hand while shouting.

15:01.880 --> 15:03.880
When performing MONGAECHIGI,

15:04.880 --> 15:07.880
turn and set your right foot inward 180 degrees.

15:08.880 --> 15:12.880
Cross your arms so your right arm faces upward and the left arm faces downward.

15:13.880 --> 15:15.880
Then strike both sides.

15:15.880 --> 15:18.880
When performing SONBADA KKODORO ORIUN ANPARMOK BAKKATMAKI,

15:19.880 --> 15:21.880
move your left foot close to the right foot.

15:22.880 --> 15:23.880
Set your right foot.

15:24.880 --> 15:28.880
Then perform WEN DRIKKUBI SONBADA KKODORO ORIUN ANPARMOK BAKKATMAKI.

15:29.880 --> 15:32.880
Maintain the same posture level when gathering your feet.

15:33.880 --> 15:38.880
Open your right fist and twist inward when connecting WEN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI

15:39.880 --> 15:40.880
and DOUBLEJIRUGI in succession.

15:41.880 --> 15:43.880
Transition to the other side.

15:43.880 --> 15:47.880
Then quickly connect to DOUBLEJIRUGI after WEN PYEONSUNGKUT UPBOTJIRUGI.

15:48.880 --> 15:51.880
When performing HECHOSANTEUMAKI this time,

15:52.880 --> 15:54.880
set your left foot to perform the move.

15:55.880 --> 15:57.880
When performing WEN YUPJIRUGI,

15:58.880 --> 16:01.880
move your right foot and assume the front GOASONGI posture.

16:02.880 --> 16:06.880
Pull an opponent as if to cover and pull them downward with the right hand.

16:07.880 --> 16:09.880
Then turn and set your right foot.

16:09.880 --> 16:12.880
As if to cover and pull them downward with the right hand.

16:13.880 --> 16:17.880
Then complete the YUPJIRUGI by setting your left foot and shouting.

16:18.880 --> 16:24.880
Then perform MONGAE CHIGI by turning and setting your right foot inward 180 degrees

16:25.880 --> 16:29.880
and crossing your arms with the left arm above and the right arm below.

16:30.880 --> 16:34.880
Cautions for SHIPJIN first part, taking a closer look.

16:34.880 --> 16:38.880
When performing WEN SONPADA KODURO ANPALMOK BAKATMAKI,

16:39.880 --> 16:43.880
the armpit of the assisting arm should not move away from the body.

16:44.880 --> 16:46.880
When performing HECHOSANTEUMAKI,

16:47.880 --> 16:49.880
your eyes should not be directed forward.

16:50.880 --> 16:55.880
When moving your foot to assume the front GOASONGI posture during YUPJIRUGI,

16:56.880 --> 16:58.880
your height must not change.

16:59.880 --> 17:01.880
When performing MONGAE CHIGI,

17:02.880 --> 17:09.880
the elbow must not swerve above or below and the elbows must not move back.

17:10.880 --> 17:12.880
Your chest must be closed.

17:13.880 --> 17:17.880
When performing SONPADA KODURO ANPALMOK BAKATMAKI,

17:18.880 --> 17:23.880
be careful not to let the armpit of the assisting arm move away from the body

17:24.880 --> 17:28.880
and maintain a posture so your height does not change when you gather your feet.

17:29.880 --> 17:34.880
When connecting PYEON SONGKUD OPPO JIRUGI and DOUBLE JIRUGI,

17:35.880 --> 17:38.880
be mindful of the synchronization of all moves and breathing.

17:40.880 --> 17:44.880
When changing posture from FRONT GOASONGI during YUPJIRUGI,

17:45.880 --> 17:47.880
your elevation must not change.

17:51.880 --> 17:57.880
We will now practice the moves of SHIPJIN first part in succession while watching the video.

17:58.880 --> 18:00.880
SHIPJIN

18:29.880 --> 18:31.880
SHIPJIN

18:33.880 --> 18:36.880
The key moves of SHIPJIN second part consist of

18:37.880 --> 18:40.880
SONPADA KODURO ORUN ANPALMOK BAKATMAKI

18:41.880 --> 18:43.880
When PYEON SONGKUD OPPO JIRUGI

18:47.880 --> 18:49.880
and DOUBLE JIRUGI

18:50.880 --> 18:52.880
When SONA KODURO ARERMAKI

18:54.880 --> 18:55.880
DAWI MIRGI

18:58.880 --> 18:59.880
DAWI MIRGI

19:02.880 --> 19:03.880
DAWI MIRGI

19:06.880 --> 19:07.880
SONNAL DUNG HAECHOMAKI

19:10.880 --> 19:11.880
SONNAL ARER HAECHOMAKI

19:13.880 --> 19:14.880
ARER HAECHOMAKI

19:15.880 --> 19:17.880
ARER HAECHOMAKI

19:20.880 --> 19:21.880
and GULO ORIGI

19:24.880 --> 19:25.880
GULO ORIGI

19:26.880 --> 19:27.880
GULO ORIGI

19:28.880 --> 19:42.880
When performing SONPADAK KODORO ORUN ANPARMOK BAKKATMAKKI, turn 90 degrees and set with your right foot as the axis and perform SONPADAK KODORO ORUN ANPARMOK BAKKATMAKKI.

19:42.880 --> 19:50.880
Use the left ball of your foot as an axis when turning back and setting.

19:50.880 --> 20:03.880
When connecting WEN PYEON SONGKUD OPPO JIRUGI and DOUBLE JIRUGI, open your right fist and twist inward, then transition from WEN DWIKKUBI to ORUN APKUBI.

20:03.880 --> 20:12.880
Perform WEN PYEON SONGKUD OPPO JIRUGI when the fist is completely open, then connect to DOUBLE JIRUGI.

20:13.880 --> 20:22.880
When performing WEN SONNA KODORO AREMAKKI, set your left foot and perform WEN DWIKKUBI WEN SONNA KODORO AREMAKKI.

20:22.880 --> 20:30.880
When performing PAWIMILKI, move your right foot and place your arms on the right side of your back.

20:30.880 --> 20:37.880
Gather your palms at the back, exert force on the lower abdomen and slowly push forward.

20:37.880 --> 20:45.880
At the end, your hands should elevate to your forehead, and your forehead should be visible between your hands.

20:45.880 --> 20:56.880
SONNAL DUNG HECCHO MAKKI is performed by crossing the right arm outside the left arm in front of the chest, then moving and setting the right foot.

20:56.880 --> 21:03.880
Slowly connect with SONNAL ARE HECCHO MAKKI after performing SONNAL DUNG HECCHO MAKKI.

21:03.880 --> 21:15.880
Cross the left arm outside the right arm in front of the chest from the SONNAL DUNG HECCHO MAKKI posture, then slowly perform ARE HECCHO MAKKI.

21:15.880 --> 21:24.880
When completing the SONNAL ARE HECCHO MAKKI, slowly clench both fists and direct your eyes forward.

21:24.880 --> 21:33.880
When performing ARE HECCHO MAKKI, slowly rise, extending both knees when both fists are almost clenched.

21:33.880 --> 21:40.880
Breathing and moves should coincide while keeping your eyes directed forward.

21:41.880 --> 21:47.880
CAUTIONS FOR SHIPJIN SECOND PART, TAKING A CLOSER LOOK

21:47.880 --> 21:56.880
When performing WEN SONNA GO DORO ARE MAKKI, be careful not to let the blocking left arm move outside the left leg.

21:56.880 --> 22:05.880
When PAUI MIUGI is completed, the wrist and elbow should not be straight, and both elbows must not open backwards.

22:05.880 --> 22:10.880
The torso must not swerve in one direction.

22:10.880 --> 22:20.880
When performing SONNAL DUNG HECCHO MAKKI, be careful not to let the back of the hand blade move outside the shoulder line.

22:20.880 --> 22:28.880
When performing SONNAL ARE HECCHO MAKKI, be mindful of your breathing and the moves while staring forward.

22:28.880 --> 22:35.880
When performing KULLO ORIGI, the arm must not be pulled behind past the waist. Then it is raised.

22:37.880 --> 22:43.880
We will now practice the moves of SHIPJIN SECOND PART in succession while watching the video.

22:58.880 --> 23:20.880
The key moves of SHIPJIN SECOND PART consist of PAUI MIUGI,

23:20.880 --> 23:43.880
ORIUN APCHAGI, CHET DARI JIRUGI, WEN APCHAGI, CHET DARI JIRUGI, ORIUN APCHAGI, and ORIUN DUNG JUMOK GO DORO APCHAGI.

23:44.880 --> 23:53.880
When performing ORIUN APCHAGI, hold both hands and pull to the left from the PAUI MIUGI posture.

23:53.880 --> 23:59.880
Then perform APCHAGI along with CHAGEUN DOLJEOGI.

23:59.880 --> 24:11.880
APCHAGI and DANGYO CHAGEUN DOLJEOGI must be performed simultaneously, and both arms being pulled along with the kicking foot must be harmonious in force and speed.

24:12.880 --> 24:21.880
When performing ORIUN CHET DARI JIRUGI, complete the move by twisting the back the moment the right heel touches the ground from the left back.

24:22.880 --> 24:32.880
When performing ORIUN DUNG JUMOK GO DORO APCHAGI, the foot that performed ORIUN APCHAGI must move forward more than one step and perform JITJIGI.

24:33.880 --> 24:36.880
Next, assume the ORIUN DWIKKOWA SEOGI posture.

24:37.880 --> 24:39.880
You must shout while this is done.

24:42.880 --> 24:46.880
Cautions for SHIPJIN third part, taking a closer look.

24:47.880 --> 24:53.880
When performing APCHAGI, be careful not to pull both fists for CHAGEUN DOLJEOGI and then kick.

24:54.880 --> 25:02.880
Both arms should be raised to the same elevation for CHET DARI JIRUGI, and the space between the fists should not be too wide nor narrow.

25:03.880 --> 25:09.880
When performing DUNG JUMOK GO DORO APCHAGI, the back of the hand of the assisting arm should not face upward.

25:12.880 --> 25:17.880
We will now practice the moves of SHIPJIN third part in succession while watching the video.

25:17.880 --> 25:41.880
The key moves of SHIPJIN fourth part consist of BAOIMIRGI.

25:47.880 --> 26:14.880
When performing PYEON SON EOK GORO ARE MAGI, assume the WEN BEOM SEOGI posture while pulling the left foot.

26:14.880 --> 26:19.880
Both hands start at the right waist, then cross the right arm over the left arm.

26:20.880 --> 26:24.880
Cautions for SHIPJIN fourth part, taking a closer look.

26:25.880 --> 26:31.880
When performing PYEON SON EOK GORO ARE MAGI, be careful not to let the elbow open.

26:32.880 --> 26:39.880
When performing SON NA DUNG GO DORO MAGI, the palm of the assisting hand should not face upward.

26:39.880 --> 26:47.880
We will now practice the moves of SHIPJIN fourth part in succession while watching the video.

26:47.880 --> 27:11.880
